{"parentUuid":"bf67dcb5-0651-4ac3-8dbc-93c57658fc68","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFqLeL5nsvr7Rpeyztyw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I made two more graphics commits on `hedgerow-grass`. Both are small, subtle changes. They were checked in a headless browser on the real GPU, the node checks pass, and both merge cleanly into `hedgerow-poc`. Nothing is pushed.\n\n- **b83485ae, light through the grass blades:** the meadow grass now lets light through the way the tree leaves already did. Under a flare, the grass tips facing it lighten a little. Grass in a wreck's shadow correctly stays dark. It costs nothing measurable.\n- **63fde205, specular anti-aliasing on the wet ground:** far-off wet cobbles had sharp highlights that flickered from pixel to pixel. The terrain now spreads those highlights a little where the surface detail is finer than a pixel, so distant cobbles show a steady sheen while close ones keep their sharp glints and puddles keep their mirror. The gain is small, because the anti-aliasing pass already handled most of the flicker: in a still view the far cobbles shimmer about 4% less frame to frame.\n\nThese last two rounds are giving smaller visible returns than the earlier ones. The bigger remaining gaps toward a Call of Duty / Medal of Honor look are in the soldiers, the weapon models and the camera. Those live in `character.js`, `player.js` and `camera.js`, which the hand-off told me not to touch because the original session is converting the game to first person in them.\n\nThe branch is now 35 commits ahead of `hedgerow-poc`, and the shared notes list them all. The test server, the headless browser and my `launch.json` entry are all removed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":235,"cache_read_input_tokens":851003,"output_tokens":530,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":235,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":530,"cache_read_input_tokens":851003,"cache_creation_input_tokens":235,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":235},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"f272e2cd-88d7-495a-ba16-076f2245aea7","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgFqLdgtDiQ7VZtFhQgef","requestRef":"150935ca-3770-4984-a4f6-c9f9ec97ed1e","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"efebe058-702b-4db3-bc92-86b71211b63c","timestamp":"2026-10-21T18:12:11.356Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"hedgerow-poc","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
