{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","hash":"ef7157c1cb55bb038df5227b6d8337a51f424fa227cf2aae82a8315c433ab9c2","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The bleach bypass effect creates a striking silvery look on the street scene but crushes the darker night scene's meadow and forest into murk, hurting readability. Since choosing between this look and the current warmth is an art-direction decision, I'll revert the change and log the finding rather than decide unilaterally.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01E9CgK2j38JfoUpcJkdJSng","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass && git checkout fun/hedgerow/js/post.js && git status --short && echo reverted","description":"Revert the bleach-bypass experiment"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013gQAANRQH317611zejmS4e","name":"Edit","input":{"file_path":"/Users/vojta/Library/Application REDACTED.md","old_string":"cobbles beside it in A/B captures; not worth the shader cost and complexity.\n","new_string":"cobbles beside it in A/B captures; not worth the shader cost and complexity.\nTried and left out (a taste call for the user): a bleach-bypass grade in post.js (desaturate the\nmid tones, contrast about mid grey). At 0.35 the street gets a silvery Saving-Private-Ryan look,\nbut the night frame sits mostly below mid grey, so the meadow and forest went murky; a lower\npivot would be needed. Left the grade as it was.\nChecked: low and medium quality presets compile and render all the new effects through their\nfallbacks (no late pass: rain/flames/plumes/fireballs with the scene; window light and rain sheets\noff); no shader errors.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
