{"parentUuid":"ac803bc9-b0f7-4c4f-a687-71ed3ae544d0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFqucJU5fPxcnkPc5EFn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This round added one commit on `hedgerow-grass`, plus a quality-preset check and one experiment I left out. The commit was checked in a headless browser on the real GPU, the node checks pass, and it merges cleanly into `hedgerow-poc`. Nothing is pushed.\n\n- **5856e8e0, rain beaded on the lit windows:** within about 3 m, a lit window in the rain is now covered in water beads. Each bead acts as a small lens showing the room behind it, bent and brighter at its rim, and now and then one runs down the glass.\n  - My first two attempts showed nothing: a real raindrop is a pixel or two at that distance, and I was shifting the view through the glass rather than bending it.\n  - The final version uses beads about a centimetre across, bends the view direction, and fades out where the beads would be smaller than a pixel.\n- **Quality presets checked:** with all the new effects, the medium and low presets still compile and render, with no shader errors. On low, which has no post-processing chain, the rain, flames, smoke plumes and fireballs draw with the scene, and the window glow and distant rain sheets switch off. The setting is back on high.\n- **Tried and left out: a \"Saving Private Ryan\" bleach-bypass colour grade.** It gave the street a silvery war-film look, but it crushed the darker meadow and forest into murk. Trading the current warm grade for that look is an art-direction call for you, so I left the grade unchanged.\n\nThe soldiers turned out to use two baked materials, so their shading is within reach in `materials.js`. But at typical combat distances they already read as clear silhouettes, so I didn't change them.\n\nThe branch is now 36 commits ahead of `hedgerow-poc`, and the shared notes list them all, including the failed experiments. The test server, the headless browser and my `launch.json` entry are all removed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":247,"cache_read_input_tokens":898942,"output_tokens":609,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":247,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":609,"cache_read_input_tokens":898942,"cache_creation_input_tokens":247,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":247},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"6d0d54a8-5d27-45d5-b646-7406e863de53","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgFqubcnQ8GaCFnazCuKT","requestRef":"5d2f821c-a931-4a74-92f9-86837b922c3e","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"c72115bd-fcea-4d02-98f4-f8da054b131a","timestamp":"2026-10-21T18:19:39.313Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"hedgerow-poc","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
