{"parentUuid":"b33851b0-9063-4394-8d29-559828c09df4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFrGJWEEaDedUr52kruE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NxaH4zvMJkKvtgFjLWmTT8","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow && python3 - <<'EOF'\np = 'README.md'\ns = open(p).read()\nold = \"\"\"    light wrapping past the shadow's edge, reddest; the hands on the rifle\n    included); round a fire, the charred\"\"\"\nassert s.count(old) == 1, s.count(old)\ns = s.replace(old, \"\"\"    light wrapping past the shadow's edge, reddest; the hands on the rifle\n    included), and their wool, found by its baked roughness, darkening in\n    the rain but never glossy, with a fabric's sheen at grazing angles;\n    round a fire, the charred\"\"\")\nopen(p, 'w').write(s)\nprint('ok')\nEOF\nfor t in world-check lod-check distance-check ai-check fp-check clutter-check character-check; do printf \"%s: \" $t; node tests/$t.mjs 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-60; done; cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass && git status --short && git add fun/hedgerow/js/materials.js fun/hedgerow/README.md && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nHedgerow graphics: wool that stays wool in the rain\n\nThe uniforms - the sleeves on the rifle in every frame, the soldiers'\ntunics - turned glossy in the rain, like wet plastic: the weather made\neverything smoother as it soaked. Wool soaks dark, not shiny. Now the\nsoldiers' atlases find their wool (what is baked rough, roughness over\n~0.75, and no metal: not the helmet, the leather, the buckles or the\nskin; SKIN_UNIFORMS.uSkinDebug 2 shows it green) and keep it matte in\nthe rain (roughness never under 0.72 there) while it still darkens, and\ngive it a fabric's sheen: a soft glow of the light at grazing angles\nalong its folds and silhouette (Charlie distribution with Neubelt\nvisibility, as three's own sheen; its colour a little of the wool's,\nlightened). Under a street lamp the sleeve loses its plastic highlight\nand reads as cloth.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -1 && (git merge-tree --write-tree --name-only hedgerow-poc hedgerow-grass >/dev/null 2>&1 && echo \"merges cleanly into hedgerow-poc\" || echo \"merge conflicts\")","description":"Run checks and commit the wool shading"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1012,"cache_read_input_tokens":928711,"output_tokens":1205,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":196},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1012,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1205,"cache_read_input_tokens":928711,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1012,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1012},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01NxaH4zvMJkKvtgFjLWmTT8":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow && python3 - <<'EOF'\np = 'README.md'\ns = open(p).read()\nold = \"\"\"    light wrapping past the shadow's edge, reddest; the hands on the rifle\n    included); round a fire, the charred\"\"\"\nassert s.count(old) == 1, s.count(old)\ns = s.replace(old, \"\"\"    light wrapping past the shadow's edge, reddest; the hands on the rifle\n    included), and their wool, found by its baked roughness, darkening in\n    the rain but never glossy, with a fabric's sheen at grazing angles;\n    round a fire, the charred\"\"\")\nopen(p, 'w').write(s)\nprint('ok')\nEOF\nfor t in world-check