{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","id":"d130fd01-77d7-4bbd-b7ad-4382118744d8","timestamp":"2026-10-21T18:24:56.865Z","version":"2.1.304","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"aca1d33e67df77c08846866245a8b157faabfdb8617ed3a1eb9cac3e5556c296","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"max"}},"base":"00cab97a-3e81-423f-963e-89cd356cc6ec","keep":1860,"tail":["f5d951e6940c8960655a9caeb34b9c22857df7d4e91263dcd3c36d0cb9901f88","f572a9940d835452ed557caa7475ea7e000b3b4d8efec61e2ec138fdd5f14552","7d46798a35b728df4ce6449684833c202f8b8abde1b2ec347d2f0a70b1391d6b"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",1862,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"a31ea685adb45c815986a1cc03720b07de003edf92b693a1daaff75a6cc7f293"}
{"parentUuid":"2586113f-4662-4f66-993a-96569ccd71bb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFrKVNB85aduSbYjGBik","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This round went into the soldiers, which I'd flagged as a gap. It turned out part of it is reachable without the off-limits files: `character.js` loads its materials through `materials.js`, so the shading could change there alone. Two commits on `hedgerow-grass`, both checked in a headless browser on the real GPU. The node checks pass, including the character check, both merge cleanly into `hedgerow-poc`, and nothing is pushed.\n\n- **de580ca6, skin that scatters light:** the hands on the rifle, which are in every frame, and the soldiers' faces were shaded like painted plastic. Skin is now picked out of the soldiers' texture by its colour; a debug view confirmed it marks the hands and face but not the uniform. It's lit with soft, slightly red edges where light falls off, a faint red glow when lit from behind, and a less glossy finish. Side-lit by a street lamp, the hands go from tan plastic to something that reads as skin.\n- **f3957912, wool that stays wool in the rain:** the rain logic made everything glossier as it got wet, so the sleeves (also in every frame) shone like wet plastic. Wool is now found by its texture's roughness and the fact it isn't metal, which tells it apart from the similar-coloured helmet. It still darkens in the rain but stays matte, and gets a soft fabric sheen at grazing angles. Under a lamp the sleeve lost its plastic highlight.\n\nI couldn't get a good close-up of an enemy soldier, because the AI kept walking them out of shot, but they share the same material.\n\nThe branch is now 38 commits ahead of `hedgerow-poc`, and the shared notes list them all. The test server, the headless browser and my `launch.json` entry are all removed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":256,"cache_read_input_tokens":932894,"output_tokens":575,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":256,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":575,"cache_read_input_tokens":932894,"cache_creation_input_tokens":256,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":256},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"66e2f941-a197-4b7d-bbad-4de9f47aee9a","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgFrKUkhiVokBCBYF51tj","requestRef":"d130fd01-77d7-4bbd-b7ad-4382118744d8","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"cfe2791c-44ea-4d41-8283-3b47242c6e72","timestamp":"2026-10-21T18:25:03.186Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"hedgerow-poc","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
