{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","hash":"fdab64a76fdcf915567ea10e32b7d3e73e1095b97794afa4ec2067be1ffb800a","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'll reduce direct specular highlights from the key and rim lights across all materials, since a rain-clouded night sky shouldn't glint on the wet mud—while keeping their diffuse contribution and preserving specular glints from lamps, fires, and the flare.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VdrnrkQ1MkZGUp6p2EnifP","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass && python3 - <<'EOF'\ns = open('assets/vendor/three/three.module.min.js', encoding='utf-8').read()\ni = s.find('reflectedLight.directSpecular += irradiance * BRDF_GGX')\nprint(i, repr(s[i:i+140]))\nprint(s.count('reflectedLight.directSpecular += irradiance * BRDF_GGX'))\nj = s.find('lights_physical_pars_fragment')\nprint(repr(s[j-40:j+60]))\nEOF","description":"Find the exact specular line in three's physical lighting chunk"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
