{"parentUuid":"5d7d911e-6277-4960-b4aa-9a4c094f4927","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFs62SBfwQQK9UDCRHmn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The rifle keeps its sheen now, while the white hot spot on the mud and the glitter on the trees stay gone. Running the checks and committing."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1208,"cache_read_input_tokens":868010,"output_tokens":1264,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":87},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1208,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1264,"cache_read_input_tokens":868010,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1208,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1208},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"c4d30491-136e-4a29-b4c8-2ebf9869366f","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgFs61py8u95zoQKfPy3T","requestRef":"9250046c-9d1e-467a-9a0e-20b48d56210b","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"a3cba0b8-3d2e-42be-8dcf-0884bd3b9c0a","timestamp":"2026-10-21T18:35:03.593Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"hedgerow-poc","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
{"parentUuid":"a3cba0b8-3d2e-42be-8dcf-0884bd3b9c0a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFs62SBfwQQK9UDCRHmn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KdBjso8tzeGSzPZMMHZEaL","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow && python3 - <<'EOF'\np = 'README.md'\ns = open(p).read()\nold = \"\"\"    `flares.js` (illumination flares: a far light for the haze and the\"\"\"\nassert s.count(old) == 1, s.count(old)\ns = s.replace(old, \"\"\"    `fill.js` (the night's fill lights — the low key light from the last of\n    the sun, the rim light of the overcast — model shapes but make no\n    glints on the world: their direct specular is cut to a tenth on the\n    ground, water, walls and leaves, where they made a sun on the puddles\n    under a sky with no sun; the soldiers and their weapons keep it),\n    `flares.js` (illumination flares: a far light for the haze and the\"\"\")\nopen(p, 'w').write(s)\nprint('ok')\nEOF\nfor t in world-check lod-check distance-check ai-check fp-check clutter-check character-check; do printf \"%s: \" $t; node tests/$t.mjs 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-60; done; cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass && git status --short && git add fun/hedgerow/js/fill.js fun/hedgerow/js/terrain.js fun/hedgerow/js/materials.js fun/hedgerow/js/grass.js fun/hedgerow/js/clutter.js fun/hedgerow/js/main.js fun/hedgerow/README.md && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nHedgerow graphics: no sun glinting on the puddles at night\n\nOn glossy wet ground the scene's fill lights made a sharp, white-hot\nglint - a blown-out sun on the mud of the forest clearing, white glitter\non the wet leaves of the meadow's trees - under a rain-clouded night\nsky with no sun in it. They are directional lights (the key light from\nthe last of the sun low over the horizon, the rim light of the\novercast), there to model shapes; the glow of the horizon is in the\nreflections already (the environment map, ssr.js). Now their direct\nspecular is cut to a tenth on the world (fill.js, new: three's physical\nlighting chunk patched so a directional light from either fill light's\ndirection - matched against their directions, set each frame from\nlights.js - keeps a tenth of its glint; applied last in the terrain,\nthe palette and baked materials, the water, the grass and the ground\nclutter), while their diffuse light, and the glints of the lamps, the\nfires, a flare and lightning, stay. The soldiers and their weapons keep\nthe fill light's sheen: it models their shape in the dark (the rifle).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -1 && (git merge-tree --write-tree --name-only hedgerow-poc hedgerow-grass >/dev/null 2>&1 && echo \"merges cleanly into hedgerow-poc\" || echo \"merge conflicts\")","description":"Run checks and commit the fill-glint fix"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1208,"cache_read_input_tokens":868010,"output_tokens":1264,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":87},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1208,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1264,"cache_read_input_tokens":868010,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1208,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1208},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01KdBjso8tzeGSzPZMMHZEaL":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow && python3 - <<'EOF'\np = 'README.md'\ns = open(p).read()\nold = \"\"\"    `flares.js` (illumination flares: a far light for the haze and the\"\"\"\nassert s.count(old) == 1, s.count(old)\ns = s.replace(old, \"\"\"    `fill.js` (the night's fill lights — the low key light from the last of\n    the sun, the rim light of the overcast — model shapes but make no\n    glints on the world: their direct specular is cut to a tenth on the\n    ground, water, walls and leaves, where they made a sun on the puddles\n    under a sky with no sun; the soldiers and their weapons keep it),\n    `flares.js` (illumination flares: a far light for the haze and the\"\"\")\nopen(p, 'w').write(s)\nprint('ok')\nEOF\nfor t in world-check lod-check distance-check ai-check fp-check clutter-check character-check; do printf \"%s: \" $t; node tests/$t.mjs 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-60; done; cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass && git status --short && git add fun/hedgerow/js/fill.js fun/hedgerow/js/terrain.js fun/hedgerow/js/materials.js fun/hedgerow/js/grass.js fun/hedgerow/js/clutter.js fun/hedgerow/js/main.js fun/hedgerow/README.md && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nHedgerow graphics: no sun glinting on the puddles at night\n\nOn glossy wet ground the scene's fill lights made a sharp, white-hot\nglint - a blown-out sun on the mud of the forest clearing, white glitter\non the wet leaves of the meadow's trees - under a rain-clouded night\nsky with no sun in it. They are directional lights (the key light from\nthe last of the sun low over the horizon, the rim light of the\novercast), there to model shapes; the glow of the horizon is in the\nreflections already (the environment map, ssr.js). Now their direct\nspecular is cut to a tenth on the world (fill.js, new: three's physical\nlighting chunk patched so a directional light from either fill light's\ndirection - matched against their directions, set each frame from\nlights.js - keeps a tenth of its glint; applied last in the terrain,\nthe palette and baked materials, the water, the grass and the ground\nclutter), while their diffuse light, and the glints of the lamps, the\nfires, a flare and lightning, stay. The soldiers and their weapons keep\nthe fill light's sheen: it models their shape in the dark (the rifle).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -1 && (git merge-tree --write-tree --name-only hedgerow-poc hedgerow-grass >/dev/null 2>&1 && echo \"merges cleanly into hedgerow-poc\" || echo \"merge conflicts\")","description":"Run checks and commit the fill-glint fix"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"c4d30491-136e-4a29-b4c8-2ebf9869366f","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgFs61py8u95zoQKfPy3T","requestRef":"9250046c-9d1e-467a-9a0e-20b48d56210b","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"3be0329e-e796-4e00-b1b0-16fe46aee70b","timestamp":"2026-10-21T18:35:12.936Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"hedgerow-poc","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
