{"parentUuid":"5d23f896-3176-4174-a065-e381fb9dd2b7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFsC1ZkkWWD7fYQR2Qmg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I followed up on both open items. The enemy close-up is now verified, and touring the forest found a real flaw, which I fixed. One commit on `hedgerow-grass`, checked in a headless browser on the real GPU. The node checks pass, low, medium and high quality all compile cleanly, it merges cleanly into `hedgerow-poc`, and nothing is pushed.\n\n- **Enemy close-up verified:** I froze the AI and placed the camera directly in front of one soldier from a test script, without touching `camera.js`. The skin and wool shading from last round apply to enemies too: the face is less plastic-orange, and the tunic's hard shoulder highlight becomes a soft cloth sheen.\n- **751e9695, no sun glinting on the puddles at night:** in the forest clearing the wet mud had a blown-out white hot spot, and wet tree leaves glittered white. The cause is the dim directional \"last of the sun\" fill light, which made sharp glints on anything glossy.\n  - Its glints are now cut to a tenth on the ground, water, walls, leaves and grass (new `fill.js`). Its soft light, and the glints from lamps, fires, flares and lightning, are unchanged. The street looks the same; the clearing and the meadow trees lost the false glints.\n  - A first version also took the sheen off the rifle in the dark, so soldiers and weapons are excluded.\n  - It works by patching a line of three.js's built-in lighting code; if a future three.js changes that line, the fix silently switches off. That's noted in the shared notes.\n- **Weapons:** the Garand's texture already has walnut grain, and its dull dark metal matches the real rifle's matte finish. Better guns would need new models, so I didn't change them.\n- **Tried and reverted: lens smudges lit by bright lights.** In this hazy scene they read as a bigger blotchy glow around the lights rather than smudges on a lens, and blurred the area around the fires.\n\nThe branch is now 39 commits ahead of `hedgerow-poc`, and the shared notes list them all. The test server, the headless browser and my `launch.json` entry are all removed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":256,"cache_read_input_tokens":873338,"output_tokens":705,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":256,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":705,"cache_read_input_tokens":873338,"cache_creation_input_tokens":256,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":256},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"6ee73026-1315-46c3-8935-cd1deccffc36","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgFsC11GwSJrzv5PAtzYn","requestRef":"83bd302e-5e77-4f1d-8ea3-5f7ee2f086f0","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"60d3bbe8-2f65-47ac-b371-46d2b3a750f5","timestamp":"2026-10-21T18:36:29.875Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"hedgerow-poc","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
