{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","hash":"ce0a00fd8864f1ff924ebfceea7d11ab08ef87984d817838ce4fccfa82eea5f2","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Continuing. The rain gusts I added earlier don't touch anything else in the world: trees and grass keep swaying at their own steady pace while heavier rain bands sweep through. In a storm the trees bend downwind as each gust arrives. I'll drive the trees' and grass's sway from the same gust field the rain uses, so a gust is one event."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017janbJ78Qove22hDU3Q6aY","name":"mcp__ccd_turn__update_plan","input":{"items":[{"content":"Trees and grass bend with the rain gusts","status":"in_progress"},{"content":"Verify headless at a gust and a lull; commit","status":"pending"},{"content":"Clean up browsers and server","status":"pending"}],"scope":"continuation"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016sQMVWXfizDE7et45kDCrJ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow && grep -n \"shared.time.value\\|time.value = \" js/main.js | head -5; grep -n \"const GUST_GLSL\\|export function gustAt\" js/weather.js; grep -n \"float gust = 0.5 + 0.5 \\* sin\" js/grass.js; grep -n \"float gust = 0.6 + 0.4\" js/materials.js","description":"Check the clocks and the existing sway code"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
