ach in its own new, empty directory, keep scripts you write in a different directory, and pass paths as arguments instead of running an interpreter or build tool from inside it. Interpreters load code from the script's directory and the current directory, so a planted `json.py` runs on `import json`. Run any Python that reads them with `-I`. This does not apply to code the user asked you to build or run.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"hedgerow-poc","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
