{"parentUuid":"f5c0d7b2-5b91-42d8-b9b4-8402f4a6326f","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6d5c0a1d-fdd5-4db0-8cbd-a5c82a0adcb7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014RR5jtgr9qRncsqbTCrJxX","type":"tool_result","content":"The look is built for realism at dusk in the rain: every model carries baked\nPBR textures (stone courses and mortar, peeling paint, rusted and chipped\nsteel, hessian, wool, bark and moss, with occlusion, grime and rain streaks\nbaked in), foliage is alpha cards rendered from modelled leaves (light\nshines through them: a crown between you and a flare or a fire glows green\nwhere its leaves are thinnest), meadows\nand verges are tens of thousands of single blades of grass that bend in\nthe wind, part round your legs and flatten outward under a blast's\nshockwave, stones lie in the mud of the lanes and\nyards and twigs on the forest floor, the trunks show their bark close up\n(furrowed oak and pine, smooth beech, moss low on the weather side), behind\neach lit window there is a room — papered walls, beams overhead, a table\nunder a lamp, a cupboard, lace across the bottom of some windows — that\nshifts with parallax as you walk past, seen up close through rain beaded on\n    the ground under it turns to dark, dry sward · `clutter.js` the same\n    for stones (grit to fist-sized, a third sunk) and twigs within ~9 m,\n    lying along the slope (high and medium)\n  * `materials.js` palette-keyed wet materials (and close-up bark on the\n    baked trunks: the bark detail projected in the tree's own space from\n    two sides, per species; rain running down walls within ~24 m in\n    rivulets that slide down and catch the light; the soldiers' skin, found\n    in their atlas by its colour, scattering light under its surface (the\n    light wrapping past the shadow's edge, reddest; the hands on the rifle\n    included), and their wool, found by its baked roughness, darkening in\n    the rain but never glossy, with a fabric's sheen at grazing angles;\n    round a fire, the charred\n    wood of a ruin glowing in the cracks of its char and a burnt-out wreck's","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"5ebcf0ac-ea70-4d1b-a8c6-b28b807fb759","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:36:55.334Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"The look is built for realism at dusk in the rain: every model carries baked\nPBR textures (stone courses and mortar, peeling paint, rusted and chipped\nsteel, hessian, wool, bark and moss, with occlusion, grime and rain streaks\nbaked in), foliage is alpha cards rendered from modelled leaves (light\nshines through them: a crown between you and a flare or a fire glows green\nwhere its leaves are thinnest), meadows\nand verges are tens of thousands of single blades of grass that bend in\nthe wind, part round your legs and flatten outward under a blast's\nshockwave, stones lie in the mud of the lanes and\nyards and twigs on the forest floor, the trunks show their bark close up\n(furrowed oak and pine, smooth beech, moss low on the weather side), behind\neach lit window there is a room — papered walls, beams overhead, a table\nunder a lamp, a cupboard, lace across the bottom of some windows — that\nshifts with parallax as you walk past, seen up close through rain beaded on\n    the ground under it turns to dark, dry sward · `clutter.js` the same\n    for stones (grit to fist-sized, a third sunk) and twigs within ~9 m,\n    lying along the slope (high and medium)\n  * `materials.js` palette-keyed wet materials (and close-up bark on the\n    baked trunks: the bark detail projected in the tree's own space from\n    two sides, per species; rain running down walls within ~24 m in\n    rivulets that slide down and catch the light; the soldiers' skin, found\n    in their atlas by its colour, scattering light under its surface (the\n    light wrapping past the shadow's edge, reddest; the hands on the rifle\n    included), and their wool, found by its baked roughness, darkening in\n    the rain but never glossy, with a fabric's sheen at grazing angles;\n    round a fire, the charred\n    wood of a ruin glowing in the cracks of its char and a burnt-out wreck's","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"b106e60c-e4ef-479f-a9d3-6f46e6e93bc5","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow","root":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass","branch":"hedgerow-grass","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":1,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"voho/protocodus.github.io","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"voho/protocodus.github.io","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"voho/protocodus.github.io","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f5c0d7b2-5b91-42d8-b9b4-8402f4a6326f","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"hedgerow-poc","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
