{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","hash":"63faf985575cd7080ed00eb2e658ca4a87be9f9400f0a1dbef068f9ad59c6a38","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'll enforce a minimum streak width of ~1.5 px so distant tracers stay visible, letting additive streaks retain most of their brightness when widened while alpha-blended ones spread theirs instead.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01ByMjgDc7kDPTeszYNcc69d","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow && grep -n \"uScreen\" js/effects.js | head -5 && python3 - <<'PY'\np='js/effects.js'\ns=open(p).read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(a)==1, (s.count(a), a)\n    s=s.replace(a,b)\nrep(\"\"\"uniform int uLightCount;\nvarying vec2 vUv;\nvarying vec4 vColor;\nvarying float vFog;\"\"\", \"\"\"uniform int uLightCount;\nuniform vec2 uScreen;\nvarying vec2 vUv;\nvarying vec4 vColor;\nvarying float vFog;\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"  float sl = length(aStretch);\n  if (sl > 1e-4) {\n    vec3 axis = aStretch / sl;\n    vec3 toCam = normalize(cameraPosition - p);\n    vec3 side = normalize(cross(axis, toCam));\n    wp = p + side * q.x * size + axis * q.y * (sl + size);\n  } else {\"\"\", \"\"\"  float sl = length(aStretch);\n  float widen = 1.0;\n  if (sl > 1e-4) {\n    vec3 axis = aStretch / sl;\n    vec3 toCam = normalize(cameraPosition - p);\n    vec3 side = normalize(cross(axis, toCam));\n    // a streak is never thinner than a pixel and a half: a tracer a hundred metres off is still\n    // a line of fire (a few centimetres wide, it would fall between the pixels)\n    float px = 2.0 * max(-(viewMatrix * vec4(p, 1.0)).z, 0.05) * uScreen.y / projectionMatrix[1][1];\n    float w = max(size, 1.5 * px);\n    widen = w / size;\n    wp = p + side * q.x * w + axis * q.y * (sl + size);\n  } else {\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"  vColor = aColor;\n  if (uLit > 0.5) {\"\"\", \"\"\"  vColor = aColor;\n  // widened, a burning streak keeps most of its light (it is far brighter than its size), a\n  // streak of dirt spreads its cover over the width\n  if (uLit > 0.5) vColor.a /= widen; else vColor.rgb *= pow(widen, -0.35);\n  if (uLit > 0.5) {\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\nnode --check js/effects.js && echo ok","description":"Give particle streaks a minimum pixel width"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
