{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","hash":"665ea726a77fcd0cc8cb9d154f877faaa8d971375b9a784f23d14816eba21b9b","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GpYjCa4UQrTPNa5MPYF9x4","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow && python3 - <<'PY'\np='README.md'\ns=open(p).read()\na=\"\"\"    cool; blasts throw up a\n    column of earth and roll dust along the ground), `flames.js` (the\"\"\"\nb=\"\"\"    cool; blasts throw up a\n    column of earth and roll dust along the ground; tracers and sparks never\n    thinner than a pixel and a half, so fire from a hundred metres off is\n    still an unbroken line), `flames.js` (the\"\"\"\nassert s.count(a)==1; s=s.replace(a,b)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\ncd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass && git add fun/hedgerow/README.md fun/hedgerow/js/effects.js && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nHedgerow graphics: tracer fire that stays a line at range\n\nParticle streaks were drawn at their true width: a tracer is 4.5 cm wide,\nso past ~40 m it fell between the pixels and broke into dots, and at 100 m\nit was gone (the enemy's machine guns fire from 45-110 m). Streaks are now\nat least a pixel and a half wide. Widened, a dirt streak spreads its cover\n(alpha / widen); a burning one (tracer, spark) gets brighter by the square\nroot of the widening, since its real brightness would fill the pixel. Near\nstreaks are unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -1 && git merge-tree --write-tree hedgerow-poc hedgerow-grass >/dev/null && echo \"merges cleanly into hedgerow-poc\"","description":"Commit the tracer visibility round"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
