{"parentUuid":"0e94e1e4-c43f-458a-b327-c43edd5b9d9b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFxpAHhwisTfbigPkKet","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added five more commits to `hedgerow-grass` this round. Nothing is pushed, and the branch still merges cleanly into `hedgerow-poc`. The four files you asked me to leave alone (camera, player, hud, character) are untouched.\n\n- **56efa833 – bullet holes now show.** Before this, almost no hole on a stone wall was ever visible. They were placed on the flat collision box, and the visible wall bulges a centimetre or more in front of it, which hid them. Holes, scratches and splats are now drawn 6 cm towards the eye without moving on screen. Each surface has its own look: chipped stone, splintered wood, dented metal, mud, blast scorch. There are four variants of each, with relief that catches the light.\n- **d7d61419 – no more black smoke columns on every shot.** Each muzzle flash lights the rain haze, and the distant smoke plumes were being drawn over that glow as black streaks. They are now drawn before the glow is added. Side effect: in a lamp-lit street the plume is now mostly hidden by the glow in front of it, which is what you'd really see. In the dark it looks as before.\n- **16830290 – close-up surface grain on walls, wrecks and crates.** Within 7 m, walls now show stone and plaster texture instead of going soft, and the flat grey ruin blocks read as stone. The relief only goes on rough surfaces and not under standing water, because on wet paint and puddled crate lids it glittered. It costs about 0.3–0.6 ms per frame. This one is a matter of taste; setting `GRAIN_UNIFORMS.uGrain.value = 0` in `materials.js` turns it off.\n- **4d7fab84 – real brass cases eject from the gun.** These are 3D cases from the new `casings.js`: the Garand's long case and the Thompson's short one. They tumble out lit by the muzzle flash, bounce, and the last 64 of each stay on the ground. Once the flash is gone they're barely visible at night, which is realistic. The cases appear where `player.js` puts them, so if the first-person work moves the ejection port, the `shell()` call there needs to follow.\n- **d2cb29be – tracers stay visible at range.** At 60 m a tracer used to break into dots, and at 100 m it vanished, which is where enemy machine guns fire from. They're now unbroken bright lines at those distances; close tracers are unchanged.\n\nI also tried drawing the meadow grass front to back to save time; it made no measurable difference, so I reverted it.\n\nAll three quality presets compile without shader errors and the nine node checks pass. The test server and headless browser are stopped and my `launch.json` entry is removed. Each round is logged in the shared notes file, `hedgerow-grass-session.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":593,"cache_read_input_tokens":485443,"output_tokens":916,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":593,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":916,"cache_read_input_tokens":485443,"cache_creation_input_tokens":593,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":593},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"4e818545-cd5e-4bf7-a2a4-4dbc00d9b52d","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgFxp9iyyHCcVKaKoWcH9","requestRef":"7bbc9617-d02e-4501-95ce-a0df3525b029","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"81b93355-912c-4cc8-818d-7c98cf75daf4","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19: