{"parentUuid":"f48842c9-d6d3-40f6-8516-d51003859252","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFyjdS5Mh4cfbnnxZLWb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VcTxUEhmXA5Y481y6zFLtM","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\np='README.md'\ns=open(p).read()\na=\"\"\"    the rain but never glossy, with a fabric's sheen at grazing angles;\n    round a fire, the charred\"\"\"\nb=\"\"\"    the rain but never glossy, with a fabric's sheen at grazing angles;\n    within 3 m (your own arms round the rifle, a man at arm's length) the\n    weave of that wool and the grain of the skin, laid on in the model's\n    own bind-pose space so they move with him;\n    round a fire, the charred\"\"\"\nassert s.count(a)==1; s=s.replace(a,b)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\ncd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass && git add fun/hedgerow/README.md fun/hedgerow/js/materials.js && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nHedgerow graphics: wool weave and skin grain on the arms close up\n\nThe soldier atlas (2048 px for the whole man) is stretched over the\nfirst-person arms, so the sleeves were smooth and the hands plastic. The\nskin variant now lays a close-up layer on within 3 m: the fabric weave\n(~2.5 mm) on what it already takes for wool, a fine grain on the skin,\nboth in the model's bind-pose space (they stay put as the arms move),\nthree projections blended by the bind-pose normal, relief turned onto the\nsurface with the screen-space frame. SKIN_UNIFORMS.uCloseUp scales it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -1 && git merge-tree --write-tree hedgerow-poc hedgerow-grass >/dev/null && echo \"merges cleanly into hedgerow-poc\"","description":"Commit the close-up arms detail"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":481,"c