{"parentUuid":"6aa7a78c-40c0-4c7f-bb9b-519ba3955d09","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFywfbQCdjkiNA81nLFx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YHGH2wJTPkcUh4f9a87Nn7","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow && python3 - <<'PY'\np='README.md'\ns=open(p).read()\na=\"\"\"    included), and their wool, found by its baked roughness, darkening in\"\"\"\nb=\"\"\"    included), and their wool, found by its baked roughness and its colour\n    (field grey, olive or khaki below the collar, not leather), darkening in\"\"\"\nassert s.count(a)==1; s=s.replace(a,b)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\nREDACTED; node $S/hl.mjs eval $S/reload.js >/dev/null; sleep 2; node $S/hl.mjs eval $S/boot.js >/dev/null && node $S/hl.mjs eval $S/helpers.js >/dev/null && node $S/hl.mjs eval $S/q_chk2.js | tr -d '\\n '; echo; cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass && node fun/hedgerow/tests/character-check.mjs 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-60 && git add fun/hedgerow/README.md fun/hedgerow/js/materials.js && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nHedgerow graphics: field grey that stays wool across the shoulders\n\nA third of the field-grey uniform in the axis atlas is baked at roughness\n0.5-0.7, under the wool test's 0.72, so the shoulders and upper arms were\ntaken for something smooth and turned rubbery-glossy in the rain. Leather\nis baked at 0.6-0.8, so roughness alone cannot part them; colour can. Wool\nis now also what is fairly rough (0.5+) and wool-coloured: field grey,\nolive or khaki, not a saturated brown, not black, and below the collar\n(the painted helmet is the same grey). Straps, belts, boots and the helmet\nkeep their sheen.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -1 && git merge-tree --write-tree hedgerow-poc hedgerow-grass >/dev/null && echo \"merges cleanly into hedgerow-poc\"","description":"Check compile and commit the wool classification fix"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1056,"cache_read_input_tokens":578208,"output_tokens":1295,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":371},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1056,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1295,"cache_read_input_tokens":578208,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1056,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1056},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01YHGH2wJTPkcUh4f9a87Nn7":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow && python3 - <<'PY'\np='README.md'\ns=open(p).read()\na=\"\"\"    included), and their wool, found by its baked roughness, darkening in\"\"\"\nb=\"\"\"    included), and their wool, found by its baked roughness and its colour\n    (field grey, olive or khaki below the collar, not leather), darkening in\"\"\"\nassert s.count(a)==1; s=s.replace(a,b)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\nREDACTED; node $S/hl.mjs eval $S/reload.js >/dev/null; sleep 2; node $S/hl.mjs eval $S/boot.js >/dev/null && node $S/hl.mjs eval $S/helpers.js >/dev/null && node $S/hl.mjs eval $S/q_chk2.js | tr -d '\\n '; echo; cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass && node fun/hedgerow/tests/character-check.mjs 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-60 && git add fun/hedgerow/README.md fun/hedgerow/js/materials.js && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nHedgerow graphics: field grey that stays wool across the shoulders\n\nA third of the field-grey uniform in the axis atlas is baked at roughness\n0.5-0.7, under the wool test's 0.72, so the shoulders and upper arms were\ntaken for something smooth and turned rubbery-glossy in the rain. Leather\nis baked at 0.6-0.8, so roughness alone cannot part them; colour can. Wool\nis now also what is fairly rough (0.5+) and wool-coloured: field grey,\nolive or khaki, not a saturated brown, not black, and below the collar\n(the painted helmet is the same grey). Straps, belts, boots and the helmet\nkeep their sheen.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -1 && git merge-tree --write-tree hedgerow-poc hedgerow-grass >/dev/null && echo \"merges cleanly into hedgerow-poc\"","description":"Check compile and commit the wool classification fix"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"fc76f1df-2710-4fbf-b76f-8ad0c5022ee0","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgFywerVCKNEPTF953qFy","requestRef":"af31bfe2-4e69-4505-b055-6a7bf9906a92","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"c75a5772-f6ea-4871-9efa-04f7a6d3667d","timestamp":"2026-10-21T20:05:07.929Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"REDACTED","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"hedgerow-poc","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
