{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","hash":"bdb918796e3ca51fcf06f728b4c49eb4bbea253283c0442a87f7a8b446991e74","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YCZpLMkx2hjoL3mi3WxpKE","name":"Edit","input":{"file_path":"/Users/vojta/Library/Application REDACTED.md","old_string":"  Observed, not fixed: the axis soldiers' upper sleeves are baked with low roughness, so they are\n  not taken for wool and look like glossy rubber when wet (uSkinDebug = 2 shows it). A colour-aware\n  cloth test or an atlas roughness fix would cure it.","new_string":"- 28915b17 FIX: the axis upper sleeves/shoulders (baked roughness 0.5-0.7) were not taken for wool\n  and went rubbery-glossy when wet. clothK now also = rough >= ~0.55 AND wool-coloured (not\n  saturated brown, not black, bind-pose y < 1.57 so the same-grey helmet stays steel).\n  uSkinDebug = 2 shows the classification (green wool, red skin)."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
