{"parentUuid":"c1efb900-8a61-47cc-a862-b7a26b62f5dc","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6d5c0a1d-fdd5-4db0-8cbd-a5c82a0adcb7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VsTygBZTTjUdbyraae5DwC","type":"tool_result","content":"/* Hedgerow — rain and lightning.\n\n   Rain is one instanced draw: thousands of streaks whose positions live on\n   the GPU, wrapped in a box that follows the camera, each a quad stretched\n   along its fall velocity and turned to face the view, as thin as a drop\n   but never under a pixel and a half (fainter instead). Beyond them, out\n   to ~60 m, sheets of rain: four cylinders round the eye, worked out per\n   pixel in one full-screen draw, each with streaks falling at the rain's\n   speed and slant, hidden behind what is nearer, lit by the lamps near\n   them and fading into the haze. Both come in gusts: bands of heavier rain,\n   leaning harder, sweeping across downwind (gust(), a slow noise blown\n   along at gust speed). Splashes are rings, and near the eye each\n   drop that lands throws up a crown of droplets for a moment, glittering by\n   the lamps; splashes are rings\n   that grow and fade on the ground around the player. Lightning comes in\n   flickering strokes every so often, lifting the sky and the light, and\n   schedules its thunder for the audio by distance. */\n\nimport * as THREE from 'three';\nimport { rng } from './util.js';\n\n// the gusts: how hard it is raining here now (about 0.55 .. 1.6), bands of it some 30 m across\n// blown downwind at gust speed. An integer hash, so gustAt() below gives the same on the CPU\n// (the splashes follow it)\nexport const GUST_GLSL = /* glsl */ `\nfloat gHash(vec2 p) {\n  uvec2 q = uvec2(ivec2(p) + 32768);\n  uint h = (q.x * 1597334677u) ^ (q.y * 3812015801u);\n  h = h * 747796405u + 2891336453u;\n  h ^= h >> 16u; h *= 2246822519u; h ^= h >> 13u;\n  return float(h) / 4294967295.0;\n}\nfloat gNoise(vec2 p) {\n  vec2 i = floor(p), f = fract(p);\n  f = f * f * (3.0 - 2.0 * f);\n  return mix(mix(gHash(i), gHash(i + vec2(1.0, 0.0)), f.x), mix(gHash(i + vec2(0.0, 1.0)), gHash(i + vec2(1.0, 1.0)), f.x), f.y);\n}\nfloat gust(vec2 xz, float time, vec2 wind) {\n  vec2 w = normalize(wind);\n  // stretched across the wind (a front of rain), carried along it\n  vec2 q = vec2(dot(xz, w), dot(xz, vec2(-w.y, w.x)) * 0.45) / 30.0 - vec2(time * 7.0 / 30.0, 0.0);\n  float n = gNoise(q) * 0.7 + gNoise(q * 2.3 + 5.1) * 0.3;\n  return 0.55 + 1.05 * smoothstep(0.3, 0.75, n);\n}`;\n\nfunction gHash(x, y) {\n  let h = (Math.imul((x + 32768) >>> 0, 1597334677) ^ Math.imul((y + 32768) >>> 0, 3812015801)) >>> 0;\n  h = (Math.imul(h, 747796405) + 2891336453) >>> 0;\n  h = (h ^ (h >>> 16)) >>> 0; h = Math.imul(h, 2246822519) >>> 0; h = (h ^ (h >>> 13)) >>> 0;\n  return h / 4294967295;\n}\nfunction gNoise(x, y) {\n  const ix = Math.floor(x), iy = Math.floor(y);\n  let fx = x - ix, fy = y - iy;\n  fx = fx * fx * (3 - 2 * fx); fy = fy * fy * (3 - 2 * fy);\n  const a = gHash(ix, iy), b = gHash(ix + 1, iy), c = gHash(ix, iy + 1), d = gHash(ix + 1, iy + 1);\n  return (a + (b - a) * fx) * (1 - fy) + (c + (d - c) * fx) * fy;\n}\n/* GUST_GLSL's gust() on the CPU */\nexport function gustAt(x, z, time, wx, wz) {","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"df8dce9e-c762-4eb6-a0f6-cfc6ee3805d0","timestamp":"2026-10-21T20:08:43.650Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"/* Hedgerow — rain and lightning.\n\n   Rain is one instanced draw: thousands of streaks whose positions live on\n   the GPU, wrapped in a box that follows the camera, each a quad stretched\n   along its fall velocity and turned to face the view, as thin as a drop\n   but never under a pixel and a half (fainter instead). Beyond them, out\n   to ~60 m, sheets of rain: four cylinders round the eye, worked out per\n   pixel in one full-screen draw, each with streaks falling at the rain's\n   speed and slant, hidden behind what is nearer, lit by the lamps near\n   them and fading into the haze. Both come in gusts: bands of heavier rain,\n   leaning harder, sweeping across downwind (gust(), a slow noise blown\n   along at gust speed). Splashes are rings, and near the eye each\n   drop that lands throws up a crown of droplets for a moment, glittering by\n   the lamps; splashes are rings\n   that grow and fade on the ground around the player. Lightning comes in\n   flickering strokes every so often, lifting the sky and the light, and\n   schedules its thunder for the audio by distance. */\n\nimport * as THREE from 'three';\nimport { rng } from './util.js';\n\n// the gusts: how hard it is raining here now (about 0.55 .. 1.6), bands of it some 30 m across\n// blown downwind at gust speed. An integer hash, so gustAt() below gives the same on the CPU\n// (the splashes follow it)\nexport const GUST_GLSL = /* glsl */ `\nfloat gHash(vec2 p) {\n  uvec2 q = uvec2(ivec2(p) + 32768);\n  uint h = (q.x * 1597334677u) ^ (q.y * 3812015801u);\n  h = h * 747796405u + 2891336453u;\n  h ^= h >> 16u; h *= 2246822519u; h ^= h >> 13u;\n  return float(h) / 4294967295.0;\n}\nfloat gNoise(vec2 p) {\n  vec2 i = floor(p), f = fract(p);\n  f = f * f * (3.0 - 2.0 * f);\n  return mix(mix(gHash(i), gHash(i + vec2(1.0, 0.0)), f.x), mix(gHash(i + vec2(0.0, 1.0)), gHash(i + vec2(1.0, 1.0)), f.x), f.y);\n}\nfloat gust(vec2 xz, float time, vec2 wind) {\n  vec2 w = normalize(wind);\n  // stretched across the wind (a front of rain), carried along it\n  vec2 q = vec2(dot(xz, w), dot(xz, vec2(-w.y, w.x)) * 0.45) / 30.0 - vec2(time * 7.0 / 30.0, 0.0);\n  float n = gNoise(q) * 0.7 + gNoise(q * 2.3 + 5.1) * 0.3;\n  return 0.55 + 1.05 * smoothstep(0.3, 0.75, n);\n}`;\n\nfunction gHash(x, y) {\n  let h = (Math.imul((x + 32768) >>> 0, 1597334677) ^ Math.imul((y + 32768) >>> 0, 3812015801)) >>> 0;\n  h = (Math.imul(h, 747796405) + 2891336453) >>> 0;\n  h = (h ^ (h >>> 16)) >>> 0; h = Math.imul(h, 2246822519) >>> 0; h = (h ^ (h >>> 13)) >>> 0;\n  return h / 4294967295;\n}\nfunction gNoise(x, y) {\n  const ix = Math.floor(x), iy = Math.floor(y);\n  let fx = x - ix, fy = y - iy;\n  fx = fx * fx * (3 - 2 * fx); fy = fy * fy * (3 - 2 * fy);\n  const a = gHash(ix, iy), b = gHash(ix + 1, iy), c = gHash(ix, iy + 1), d = gHash(ix + 1, iy + 1);\n  return (a + (b - a) * fx) * (1 - fy) + (c + (d - c) * fx) * fy;\n}\n/* GUST_GLSL's gust() on the CPU */\nexport function gustAt(x, z, time, wx, wz) {","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"e512d48a-deb8-423d-833e-47c3d5975f38","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow","root":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass","branch":"hedgerow-grass","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"voho/protocodus.github.io","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"voho/protocodus.github.io","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"voho/protocodus.github.io","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c1efb900-8a61-47cc-a862-b7a26b62f5dc","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"hedgerow-poc","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
